---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { repository, withBase } from '../lib/paths';
---
<Base title="About Jordan’s collection" active="about">
  <div class="container reading-page">
    <a class="back-link" href={withBase()}>← Explore the collection</a>
    <h1>One personal collection.<br /><span class="muted">Useful, inspectable work.</span></h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead">Jordan’s Agent Toolkit Collection brings together original skills, practical workflows, and selected tools for AI-assisted software engineering.</p>
      <h2>The work behind the profile</h2>
      <p>This is a home for the approaches Jordan is developing and documenting: bounded tasks, parallel work, focused testing, debugging, interface review, and evidence-backed handoffs. Individual skill pages provide direct links that can be shared from a profile or an article.</p>
      <h2>Own instructions, not renamed packages</h2>
      <p>The skills are written for this collection with AI assistance, using task requirements and concrete examples. They are not line-by-line rewrites of other skill libraries. Research helps identify useful problems; the collection develops its own procedures and evaluation cases.</p>
      <h2>How the pieces fit</h2>
      <p>Start with the <a href={withBase('skills/')}>skill collection</a>, then follow the <a href={withBase('workflows/')}>task-to-handoff workflow</a>. Selected external tools live in their <a href={withBase('tools/')}>own section</a>. A skill using a third-party tool does not claim ownership of that tool.</p>
      <h2>Evidence as the collection grows</h2>
      <p>The current skills are experimental. Examples and evaluation scenarios explain intended behavior; they are not fabricated execution results. Website tests do not establish agent-host compatibility, production usage, or productivity improvements.</p>
      <h2>Explore further</h2>
      <p>Read Jordan’s <a href="https://jdavis-software.github.io/content/articles/parallel-agent-engineering/">parallel-agent engineering article</a>, inspect the <a href={repository}>repository</a>, or suggest an improvement with a concrete use case.</p>
      <p>Authoring and provenance are documented in the <a href={`${repository}/blob/main/docs/ORIGINAL_SKILLS.md`}>original-skills guide</a> and <a href={`${repository}/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md`}>repository notices</a>. Actual reused material and dependencies retain their applicable terms. The original-content license remains unselected.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
